[{:adr/id "2607125300"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5820/6201 gain Docker packaging + CI (CI workflow push partially blocked on OAuth scope)"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/related ["2607124600-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-http-service-layer" "2607124800-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-file-store-persistence" "2607125100-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-real-model-adapter"]
  :adr/loop-context "Eighth cycle of the /loop dynamic-mode self-paced 'raise maturity toward live production operation' task."
  :adr/decision "Added multi-stage Dockerfiles to both cloud-itonami-isic-5820 and cloud-itonami-isic-6201 (JDK builder stage cloning sibling kotoba-lang/{crm,langgraph} and resolving deps; JRE runtime stage, non-root user, no secrets baked in, HEALTHCHECK on GET /health). Added .github/workflows/ci.yml to both (test job with sibling checkouts + clojure -M:dev:test/-M:lint; docker-build job; explicitly no deploy/registry-push step)."
  :adr/real-verification "Both Dockerfiles were actually built and run in this sandbox (Docker via OrbStack), not merely authored: confirmed non-root execution, curl'd /health and authenticated/unauthenticated protected endpoints against the running container, confirmed a real write operation committed and the file-store snapshot landed on a host bind mount, then cleaned up containers/images."
  :adr/oauth-scope-blocker "Pushing .github/workflows/ci.yml was rejected by GitHub: the gh CLI's OAuth token lacks the workflow scope, which GitHub requires specifically for pushes touching .github/workflows/*.yml. Attempted gh auth refresh -h github.com -s workflow, which requires a human to complete a browser-based device-code authorization -- an agent cannot complete this alone. Rather than block the otherwise-verified Dockerfile/docs changes, a follow-up commit removed ci.yml from the push (kept as an untracked file on disk in each scratch clone, ready to add once the owner grants the workflow scope)."
  :adr/pushed-commits "cloud-itonami-isic-5820: 3a3f168 (Dockerfile/docs, pushed). cloud-itonami-isic-6201: 1f3e555 (Dockerfile/docs, pushed). Neither repo's CI workflow file has landed on main yet."
  :adr/remaining-gaps "CI workflow not yet landed (owner action needed: grant workflow OAuth scope, or add the file manually via the GitHub UI); no real cloud deployment (image build/run verified locally only); no registry push; cloud-itonami-isic-6202 untouched, consistent with the standing decision to avoid it without coordination; the three original blockers (6202 coordination, real LLM credentials, deployment infra decisions) remain open."
  :adr/scope-note "New ADR covering Docker/CI packaging for both sibling actors together, since it is one coherent cross-cutting infrastructure step with a shared blocker discovery"}]
